# Code Quality Rules

## TypeScript Standards
- Use strict TypeScript with proper type annotations
- Prefer `const` and `let` over `var`
- Use arrow functions for callbacks
- Use optional chaining (`?.`) and nullish coalescing (`??`) where appropriate
- Always handle null/undefined cases explicitly
- Use meaningful variable and function names
- Keep functions focused and single-purpose

## Module Organization
- Each module should be self-contained with clear responsibilities
- Export functions, not classes unless necessary
- Use named exports over default exports
- Keep modules small and focused

## Code Style
- Use 2 spaces for indentation
- Use single quotes for strings (unless escaping)
- Add JSDoc comments for exported functions
- Keep line length reasonable (max 100 characters)
- Use trailing commas in multi-line objects/arrays

## Error Handling
- Always check for null/undefined before accessing properties
- Use try-catch for operations that might fail
- Provide meaningful error messages
- Handle edge cases gracefully

## Performance
- Avoid unnecessary DOM queries (cache selectors when possible)
- Use event delegation for dynamic content
- Debounce/throttle expensive operations
- Minimize global state

## Compatibility
- Maintain compatibility with existing Webflow HTML structure
- Support data attributes as specified
- Ensure code works with external dependencies (FsCC, Webflow, etc.)

